Relicshot - Privacy Policy

Last updated: 25 November 2026

Relicshot is a mobile puzzle game made by CodingTech Studio, Başakşehir / İstanbul, Türkiye ("we").
Contact: codingtechstudio@gmail.com

Relicshot is made for adults. It is not directed to children and we do not knowingly collect data from children.


1. What stays on your device

Your progress, stars, coins, lives, boosters, museum and settings are stored only on your device. We have no account system and no server of our own. Deleting the game deletes this data.


2. Crash reports

When the game crashes, a crash report is sent to Google Firebase Crashlytics so that we can find and fix the error. A report holds the error trace, the device model, the operating system version, the game version and an installation identifier created by Firebase. It does not hold your name, e-mail address, contacts or precise location. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in keeping the game working.


3. Play statistics

To balance the levels, the game can send game events such as "level started", "level completed", "shots used", "booster used" or "coins spent" to Google Analytics for Firebase, together with an app-instance identifier, general device information (model, operating system, language, country derived from the IP address) and the time. Events contain no name, e-mail or free text. Purchases made in the shop are counted as events too, without any payment details.

The game collects play statistics only with your consent. It asks once in its own "Play statistics" window; nothing is sent before you choose "Allow", and "No thanks" keeps them off. You can change your answer at any time under Settings > Privacy choices; if you then choose "No thanks", collection stops and the statistics data kept on your device is cleared. In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland the game does not ask and does not collect play statistics at all. The advertising identifier is not collected for statistics, and the statistics are never used for advertising: ad storage, ad user data and ad personalisation are switched off in the analytics settings.


4. Ads

The game can show ads through Google AdMob: short videos you choose to watch for a reward (extra balls, double coins, an extra life) and, from level 16 and not in your first three days, at most one full-screen ad after a won level, never during play. Any purchase in the shop turns the full-screen ads off for good. To show and measure ads, Google receives the advertising identifier of your device, your IP address (from which an approximate location is derived), device information and your interactions with the ads.

Before any ad is requested, Google's consent form asks for your choice where the law requires it (for example in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland). You can change your choice at any time under Settings > Privacy choices. You can also reset or delete the advertising identifier in your device settings.

How Google uses data from apps that use its services: https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites


5. Who receives data

Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC, as the provider of Firebase Crashlytics, Google Analytics for Firebase and AdMob. Google may process data on servers outside your country, including the United States; it relies on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. We do not sell your data and we share it with no one else.

Purchases: if you buy something in the shop, the payment is handled entirely by Google Play (or the App Store). We never see your card or payment details. The game only learns from the store which product was bought, so that it can add it to your game. "Restore purchases" in the shop asks the store again which one-time products your store account owns.


6. How long data is kept

Crash reports: 90 days. Play statistics: up to 14 months. Data on your device: until you delete the game or its data.


7. Your rights

Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR, the UK GDPR or the Turkish Law No. 6698, KVKK), you have the right to ask what data is held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict its use, to withdraw your consent at any time, and to complain to your data protection authority. Write to codingtechstudio@gmail.com. We answer within 30 days.


8. Permissions

Internet access (crash reports, statistics, ads, purchases), vibration (short feedback pulses you can switch off in Settings), the advertising identifier (ads), billing (purchases through Google Play) and the install referrer (added by Firebase to tell where the game was installed from).


9. Changes

If this policy changes, the date at the top changes and the new text is published at the same address.


